    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p124-practice-04-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$a$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For $a\\ne0$, $|a|$ controls branch steepness. The vertex is $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},c\\right)$, so changing $a$ with $b$ fixed can also move it horizontally.\n\nIf $a=0$, the graph is the horizontal line $y=\\pm|b|+c$.",
          "worked": "For $a\\ne0$, the branches have gradients $\\pm|a|$. Increasing $|a|$ makes them steeper; decreasing $|a|$ makes them less steep.\n\nThe vertex occurs where the expression inside the absolute value is zero:\n$$\\begin{align*}ax+b&=0\\\\ax&=-b\\\\x&=-\\frac{b}{a}.\\end{align*}$$\nIts height is $c$, so the vertex is $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},c\\right)$. Changing $a$ with $b$ fixed can therefore change the horizontal position as well as the steepness. When $b=0$, the vertex remains at $(0,c)$.\n\nIf $a=0$, then $f(x)=\\pm|b|+c$ for every $x$. This is a constant function, with no V-shaped vertex.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p124-practice-04-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$b$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For fixed $a\\ne0$, $b$ controls horizontal translation: the vertex has $x$-coordinate $-\\frac{b}{a}$.\n\nIf $a=0$, changing $b$ changes the constant height $\\pm|b|+c$.",
          "worked": "For fixed $a\\ne0$, the vertex satisfies $ax+b=0$, so its coordinates are $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},c\\right)$. Changing $b$ leaves the branch steepness $|a|$ and vertex height $c$ unchanged. It translates the graph horizontally.\n\nRelative to $b=0$, the horizontal displacement is $-\\frac{b}{a}$: left when $\\frac{b}{a}>0$ and right when $\\frac{b}{a}<0$.\n\nIf $a=0$, the function is $f(x)=\\pm|b|+c$. Changing $b$ changes the height of this horizontal line rather than moving a V-shaped graph horizontally.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p124-practice-04-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$c$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Translates the graph vertically by $c$: upwards if $c>0$ and downwards if $c<0$.",
          "worked": "Adding $c$ increases every output of $y=\\pm|ax+b|$ by $c$. The graph moves upwards by $c$ units when $c>0$, or downwards by $|c|$ units when $c<0$. There is no vertical shift when $c=0$.\n\nFor $a\\ne0$, the vertex moves from $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},0\\right)$ to $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},c\\right)$. The vertical-translation rule also applies when $a=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p124-practice-04-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the plus/minus sign.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For $a\\ne0$, $+$ gives an upward-opening V and $-$ a downward-opening V. Changing the sign reflects the graph in $y=c$.",
          "worked": "Since $|ax+b|\\ge0$, the graph of $y=|ax+b|+c$ lies on or above $y=c$, while the graph of $y=-|ax+b|+c$ lies on or below $y=c$.\n\nFor $a\\ne0$, both have vertex $\\left(-\\frac{b}{a},c\\right)$. The plus sign gives an upward-opening V and the minus sign a downward-opening V. At each $x$, the two graphs are equally far above and below $y=c$, so changing the sign reflects the graph in that line.\n\nIf $a=0$, the two graphs are the horizontal lines $y=c+|b|$ and $y=c-|b|$. They are also reflections in $y=c$, and coincide when $b=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
